# Narration prompt: the hidden Perception success at Harrowfield's well.
# Opened from code (MapComponent_TSC_WellWatcher) in the conversation
# window; the "NPC" is the colonist who noticed, so their portrait frames
# the moment. {PLAYER} is that same pawn.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_WellLedge

== start ==
Waiting by the well, {PLAYER} leans on the cobble rim and looks down. Then looks again.

A few feet below the rim, between the top of the shaft and the dark shine of the water, there is a *ledge*. And behind the ledge, where no light reaches, the wall does not stop. It opens.

Old vines grow down the inside of the shaft, rooted in the stone seams, thick as tarred rope.

Someone could try to jump down to the ledge, if they trust their legs (Athletics). Or trust the vines to hold a climber's weight (Nature). The first one down will not have an easy time of it. After that, the way could be rigged properly for everyone.

* [Step back from the rim.] -> end
